Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — individual review draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: Individual scene draft; whole-film pass provisionally accepted, individual author review pending

INT. RUTH'S OFFICE/POLICE EVIDENCE ROOM - DAY

Zoe rejects a proposal to "release everything." With Ruth and a police contact she identifies the altered order, North Vale's answer and the limited records needed to test them. She asks who can copy them, who can see the names and what cannot honestly be promised.

Police preserve logs, templates and routing; they obtain signed contractor and adult accounts. Mac cooperates under counsel. Cain's old channels no longer give him the same reach. None of this decides the historic cases at once.

Zoe crosses out a triumphant word in her notebook and writes IRREVERSIBLE. She closes it herself.
